# Docker rules (V4–V5)

## V4 — Optional Docker

- `DOCKER_ENABLED=false` must allow full application startup with no Docker client.
- `internal/runtime` uses `docker.NoopSource` when disabled.
- Tests run with `DOCKER_ENABLED=false` when Docker is unavailable.

## V5 — Non-blocking collection

- `internal/docker` maintains a cache updated on its own ticker.
- The main metrics loop reads `Cached()` — never calls Docker API synchronously in the collection tick.

## Docker host resolution

Follow moby client defaults: `DOCKER_HOST` env, then common socket paths (`/var/run/docker.sock`, `~/.docker/run/docker.sock` on macOS).
